%description:

Tests that the modular relay of BridgingLayer stops with an error in a switch
with STP. BridgingLayer ignores the port states that STP sets, so the switch
would forward frames on blocked ports, and a network with a loop would flood
frames around it. The network is two switches connected by two links.

%file: test.ned

import inet.linklayer.configurator.common.L2NetworkConfigurator;
import inet.node.ethernet.Eth100M;
import inet.node.ethernet.EthernetSwitch;

network TestNetwork
{
    submodules:
        l2NetworkConfigurator: L2NetworkConfigurator;
        switch1: EthernetSwitch {
            hasStp = true;
        }
        switch2: EthernetSwitch {
            hasStp = true;
        }
    connections:
        switch1.ethg++ <--> Eth100M <--> switch2.ethg++;
        switch1.ethg++ <--> Eth100M <--> switch2.ethg++;
}

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
network = TestNetwork
ned-path = .;../../../../src
sim-time-limit = 10s
*.switch*.llc.typename = "Ieee8022Llc"
*.switch1.bridging.typename = "BridgingLayer"

%exitcode: 1
%postrun-command: grep '<!>' test.out test.err > port-state-error.out || true
%contains: port-state-error.out
Interface 'eth0' has an STP/RSTP port state, which this module ignores, so it would also forward frames on blocked ports; use Ieee8021dRelay as the relay of a node with STP or RSTP
